      "message": "It feels a little weird to me to share this code between the two implementations. Really, the source format is an implementation detail - `SkPngRustCodec` *could* choose to ask Rust\u0027s `png` crate to generate a different format, which it would then feed to `skcms`. (And it\u0027s not feeding *anything* to `skcms` right now.)\n\nBut given that we intend for it to mirror `SkPngCodec`, I guess it\u0027s fine?\n\n(I also find it awkward that we store it in `SkCodec`. I\u0027m sure it made sense at the time, but it\u0027s passed in the constructor, even though it\u0027s not `const` and we have a setter and getter for it. It probably *was* `const` initially.)",
